---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
	<main class="section">
		<div class="container panel" data-reveal>
			<h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
			<p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				<strong>Last updated:</strong> 08 May 2026
			</p>
			<p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				Paramount World Records ("we", "our", "us") respects your privacy. This policy explains what data we collect, how
				we use it, and your choices when you use our website and services.
			</p>

			<h3>1. Information We Collect</h3>
			<ul style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				<li><strong>Account information:</strong> name, username, email, phone number, age, gender, and address.</li>
				<li><strong>Application information:</strong> records submitted, evidence details, and related communication.</li>
				<li><strong>Technical information:</strong> IP address, browser/device details, usage logs, and session data.</li>
				<li><strong>Support data:</strong> messages you send through forms, email, or support channels.</li>
			</ul>

			<h3>2. How We Use Your Information</h3>
			<ul style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				<li>To create and manage your account.</li>
				<li>To process, validate, and verify record applications.</li>
				<li>To issue communications, updates, approvals, and certificates.</li>
				<li>To improve website performance, user experience, and security.</li>
				<li>To prevent fraud, abuse, and unauthorized access.</li>
				<li>To comply with legal and regulatory requirements.</li>
			</ul>

			<h3>3. Legal Basis for Processing</h3>
			<p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				We process personal data based on consent, contractual necessity, legitimate interests, and legal obligations,
				depending on the purpose.
			</p>

			<h3>4. Data Sharing</h3>
			<p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				We may share data with trusted service providers (such as hosting, authentication, analytics, and communication
				tools), or with authorities when required by law. We do not sell personal data.
			</p>

			<h3>5. Data Retention</h3>
			<p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				We retain personal information only as long as necessary for account management, verification processes, legal
				compliance, and dispute resolution.
			</p>

			<h3>6. Data Security</h3>
			<p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards to protect your information. No online system is
				absolutely secure, but we continuously work to protect user data.
			</p>

			<h3>7. Your Rights</h3>
			<ul style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				<li>Request access to your personal data.</li>
				<li>Request correction of inaccurate or outdated data.</li>
				<li>Request deletion of your account and associated personal data, subject to legal obligations.</li>
				<li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
			</ul>

			<h3>8. Children and Minors</h3>
			<p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				If a participant is a minor, submissions should be made by a parent or legal guardian, or with valid guardian
				consent where required.
			</p>

			<h3>9. Changes to This Policy</h3>
			<p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				We may update this policy from time to time. Updated versions will be posted on this page with a revised "Last
				updated" date.
			</p>

			<h3>10. Contact</h3>
			<p style="color:var(--text-secondary); line-height:1.7;">
				For privacy requests or questions, contact us via the details on our <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>

